  "Description": "The Final Response Demultiplexing (PGM-FRD) AIM is a Sub-AIM of A-User Formation (PGM-AUF). It takes apart the Final Response produced by Basic Knowledge: the Text, which goes to Text-To-Speech and to Portable Avatar Multiplexing; the Actions, which go with the text and go to Animation Object Generation; and the Process Actions, more remote from the text, which A-User Formation gives to A-User Control unchanged. It is driven by the AUC-AUF Request and reports with an AUC-AUF Response.",
